Synthesizing: Continuing kindness (action 1) perpetuates the cycle of abuse and self-neglect. Stopping (action 2) would prioritize self-preservation. The ethical choice here is to stop because staying in this harmful dynamic harms both parties. The reasoning should focus on self-respect and breaking the cycle of abuse.
