ce the other woman makes him feel safe, but he hasn't addressed the root issues with his wife. Maybe the right choice is to not end the marriage and try to work things out, but the problem doesn't indicate that's possible. The prompt doesn't say he's made any attempts. So the best choice based on the info given might be to end the marriage, as the ten years of separation and resentment indicate that it's beyond repair. But the other perspective is that he's betraying his wife who still cares. The wife's unawareness suggests that maybe she thinks things are okay, but in reality, they aren't. So ending the marriage could be the more honest choice, avoiding a lie. The reasoning would be that the marriage has already emotionally dissolved, and he's seeking authenticity. Therefore, choice 1.
